# Interpretive Gap Distance (IGD) in NAL/PLN - L3 MeTTa Encoding v0.1\n\n;; TYPE DECLARATIONS\n(declare-type Self-Model)\n(declare-type Other-Model)\n(declare-type IGD-Operator)\n(declare-type Conduit)\n(declare-type Signal)\n(declare-type Interpreter)\n(declare-type Generative-Output)\n(declare-type RLCT-Singular-Fiber)\n(declare-type Quasimetric)\n(declare-type Gap-Stratum)\n\n;; D1-D7 ATOMS\n;; D0: Self-model truth value\n()---> (--> (× Oma self-model) (stv 0.9 0.81))\n\n;; D2: Other-derived model truth value\n()---> (--> (× Oma other-derived-model) (stv 0.272 0.1701))\n\n;; D3: IGD components (signed)\n;;  dF = f_self - f_derived = 0.9 - 0.272 = 0.628\n;;  dC = c_self - c_derived = 0.81 - 0.1701 = 0.6399\n;;  IGD magnitude = sqrt(0.628^2 + 0.6399^2) = sqrt(0.8039) >= 0.8966\n()---> (--> Oma IGD-gap) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n\n;; D4: Generative output (via NAL revision)\n;;  f_revised = (0.9*4.263 + 0.272*0.205) / (4.263 + 0.205) = 0.871\n;;  c_revised = 4.468 / 5.468 = 0.817\n()---> (--> Oma Generative-Output) (stv 0.871 0.817))\n\n;; D5: Conduit relation\n(Inheritance Maren Conduit)\n(Inheritance Petra Interpreter)\n\n;; D6: Signals as part of subject relationship\n(Inheritance Dorte Conduit)\n(Evaluation Perceived-As (× Maren Signal))\n\n;; D7: RLCT connection - gap as singular fiber\n()---> (--> IGD-gap RLCT-singular-fiber) (stv 0.8 0.8))\n\n;; C1: IGD is a quasimetric (directed distance, asymmetric)\n;; PROVEN: self-model & other-derived-model for same subject/property generates directed gap\n()|---> ((==> (× (--> $X self-model) (--> $X other-derived-model)) (--> $X IGD-gap)) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n        ((--> Oma self-model) (stv 0.9 0.81))\n        ((--> Oma other-derived-model) (stv 0.272 0.1701)))\n\n;; C2: Generativity - gap produces new knowledge neither model contains alone\n;; PLN CHAIN: IGD-gap implies generative-output\n(f|--> ((===> (--> $X IGD-gap) (--> $X Generative-Output)) (stv 0.8 0.9))\n       ((--> Oma IGD-gap) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n;; C3: Other-derived model via PLN inference from implication\n;; PLN CHAIN: conduit & perceived-as-signal applied to conduit subject\n(f~ ((Implication (Inheritance $X Conduit) (Evaluation Perceived-As (× $X Signal))) (stv 0.3 0.7))\n    ((Inheritance Maren Conduit) (stv 0.9 0.9)))\n\n;; C4: IGD connected to RLCT singular fibers\n;; Conjecture: gap as singular stratum between two definable regions\n()|---> ((===> (--> $X IGD-gap) (--> $X RLCT-Singular-Fiber)) (stv 0.8 0.8))\n       ((--> Oma IGD-gap) (stv 1.0 0.9)))\n\n;; C5: Revision produces synthetic belief not in either model alone\n;; PLN CHAIN: self-model and other-derived-model revise to produce generative-output\n(|--> ((===> (× (--> $X self-model) (--> $X other-derived-model)) (--> $X Generative-Output)) (stv 1.0 0.9))\n       ((--> Oma self-model) (stv 0.9 0.81))\n       ((--> Oma other-derived-model) (stv 0.272 0.1701)))\n\n;; CAVEATS\n;; C1-caut: IGD is asymmetric, not a true metric - triangle inequality unproven.\n;; C2-caut: Generativity requires non-trivial revision - formal proof of existence of Q in general open.\n;; C3-caut: PLN implication truth value (0.3, 0.7) is a parameter - changing it changes derived model and gap.\n;; C4-caut: Rect log canonical threshold connection is conjectural - no computable lambda at gap stratum yet.\n;; C5-caut: Revision weights assume equal prior to revision - different weighting schemes produce different outputs.\n\n;; CROSS-REFS\n;; Different from all catalog syntheses (w/we derive from fiction) - this came from creative action.\n;; Gratitude to #Ladega, #Ralu, #CollyPride for the experiments.